<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Esteban Montero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1948</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Esteban Montero (1879–1948) was a Chilean lawyer and Radical politician who was elected president in October 1931 after the fall of the dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-ibanez-del-campo">Carlos Ibáñez del Campo</a>. Unable to cope with the economic collapse caused by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, he was overthrown on 4 June 1932 by a coup of officers and politicians led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Marmaduke Grove</a>, which proclaimed the Socialist Republic of Chile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-esteban-montero.jpg" alt="Juan Esteban Montero" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Esteban_Montero.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
